                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Arrange the five consonants in a circle, then place A, E and I in distinct gaps.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Arrange T, R, N, G and L in a circle in $4!$ ways. There are five circular gaps. Place A, E and I in different gaps in $5\\times4\\times3$ ways.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=4!\\times5\\times4\\times3\\\\N&=24\\times60\\\\N&=1440\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the vowels are all together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p45-q9-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "5!\\times3!=720",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p45-q9-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treat the three vowels as one block and arrange the vowels within it.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Treat A, E and I as one block. The block and five consonants form six distinct objects in a circle, giving $5!$ arrangements. The vowels have $3!$ orders within their block.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=5!\\times3!\\\\N&=120\\times6\\\\N&=720\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
